<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: TABLE-AIB says H1 pre-tax profit up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-AIB says H1 pre-tax profit up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			 (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		22.3		   vs 18.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.80		   vs 5.95</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    242.2		  vs 201.1</p>
<p> Total operating income 734.0		  vs 629.5</p>
<p> Net interest income    475.5		  vs 408.7</p>
<p> Other income	     258.5		  vs 220.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Allied Irish Banks Plc said its cost/income ratio improved to 63.1 percent from 64.3 percent.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
